==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/aʊtˈdɔː(ɹ)z/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outdoors.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)z|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{compound|en|out|doors}} (plural of {{m|en|door}}), probably as a shortening of {{from|en|out of doors}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''adv.'' and ''n.''|noformat=1|id=7729124306}}</ref><ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary|passage=[1810–20; earlier ''out'' (''of'') ''doors'']}}.</ref> Alternatively, from {{suffix|en|outdoor#Adjective<pos:adjective>|s<pos:adverbial genitive suffix><id:adverbial>}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=adv}}</ref>

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# Not [[inside]] a house or under covered structure; unprotected; in the [[open]] air.
#: {{syn|en|alfresco#Adverb|withoutdoors<q:archaic>}}
#: {{ux|en|They went '''outdoors''' to light up their cigarettes.}}

